<a href="https://examprepzone.com/countries-capitals-currencies-list-pdf-bengali/" class="language-btn">বাংলা</a></div><div class="test-post-area"><nav id="toc-box" class="wp-block-rank-math-toc-block" style="display:none;"><div id="toc-header"><div id="toc-title">Table of Contents:</div>
<button id="toc-toggle">Show</button></div><div id="toc-list" style="display: none;"></div></nav><div class="epz-post"><h2>List of Countries, Capitals, and Currencies of the World <br>Static GK</h2><p>In today&#8217;s competitive examination landscape, having a clear knowledge of <strong>countries, capitals, and their currencies</strong> is essential. Over the past few years, questions from this topic have appeared regularly. For the convenience of students, we have presented this updated 2026 list of important countries, which will significantly help in boosting your General Knowledge.</p><h3>Continent-wise List of Countries, Capitals, and Currencies</h3><p>The capitals and currencies of countries vary according to the geographical and economic importance of each continent. Below, we have provided a continent-wise list of highly important countries, their capitals, and current currencies, specifically tailored for 2026 exam preparation.</p><h3>List of Asian Countries, Capitals, and Currencies</h3><p>Developing and influential countries of the Asian continent are most frequently featured in competitive exams. Below is a list of the major countries in Asia:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Country</th><th>Capital</th><th>Currency</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>India</td><td>New Delhi</td><td>Rupee</td></tr><tr><td>Bangladesh</td><td>Dhaka</td><td>Taka</td></tr><tr><td>Pakistan</td><td>Islamabad</td><td>Rupee</td></tr><tr><td>Sri Lanka</td><td>Sri Jayawardenepura Kotte</td><td>Rupee</td></tr><tr><td>Nepal</td><td>Kathmandu</td><td>Rupee</td></tr><tr><td>Bhutan</td><td>Thimphu</td><td>Ngultrum</td></tr><tr><td>Myanmar</td><td>Naypyidaw</td><td>Kyat</td></tr><tr><td>China</td><td>Beijing</td><td>Yuan / Renminbi</td></tr><tr><td>Japan</td><td>Tokyo</td><td>Yen</td></tr><tr><td>Afghanistan</td><td>Kabul</td><td>Afghani</td></tr><tr><td>Indonesia</td><td>Nusantara</td><td>Rupiah</td></tr><tr><td>Iraq</td><td>Baghdad</td><td>Dinar</td></tr><tr><td>Iran</td><td>Tehran</td><td>Rial / Toman</td></tr><tr><td>Israel</td><td>Jerusalem</td><td>Shekel</td></tr><tr><td>Saudi Arabia</td><td>Riyadh</td><td>Riyal</td></tr><tr><td>Thailand</td><td>Bangkok</td><td>Baht</td></tr><tr><td>Turkey</td><td>Ankara</td><td>Lira</td></tr><tr><td>United Arab Emirates (UAE)</td><td>Abu Dhabi</td><td>Dirham</td></tr><tr><td>South Korea</td><td>Seoul</td><td>Won</td></tr><tr><td>Maldives</td><td>Male</td><td>Rufiyaa</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="read-more-box">
<strong>Also Check:</strong> <a href="https://examprepzone.com/ramsar-sites-in-india-state-wise-list/">Ramsar Sites in India: State-wise List &#038; key facts for competitive exams</a> (Updated)</div><h3>List of European Countries, Capitals, and Currencies</h3><p>European countries are well-known for their developed economies and powerful currencies. Questions often appear in exams regarding countries using the Euro. Below is a list of the major countries in Europe:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Country</th><th>Capital</th><th>Currency</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>United Kingdom (UK)</td><td>London</td><td>Pound Sterling</td></tr><tr><td>Russia</td><td>Moscow</td><td>Ruble</td></tr><tr><td>France</td><td>Paris</td><td>Euro</td></tr><tr><td>Germany</td><td>Berlin</td><td>Euro</td></tr><tr><td>Italy</td><td>Rome</td><td>Euro</td></tr><tr><td>Spain</td><td>Madrid</td><td>Euro</td></tr><tr><td>Switzerland</td><td>Bern</td><td>Swiss Franc</td></tr><tr><td>Portugal</td><td>Lisbon</td><td>Euro</td></tr><tr><td>Norway</td><td>Oslo</td><td>Krone</td></tr><tr><td>Sweden</td><td>Stockholm</td><td>Krona</td></tr><tr><td>Denmark</td><td>Copenhagen</td><td>Krone</td></tr><tr><td>Ukraine</td><td>Kyiv</td><td>Hryvnia</td></tr><tr><td>Austria</td><td>Vienna</td><td>Euro</td></tr><tr><td>Belgium</td><td>Brussels</td><td>Euro</td></tr><tr><td>Greece</td><td>Athens</td><td>Euro</td></tr><tr><td>Finland</td><td>Helsinki</td><td>Euro</td></tr><tr><td>Vatican City</td><td>Vatican City</td><td>Euro</td></tr><tr><td>Netherlands</td><td>Amsterdam</td><td>Euro</td></tr><tr><td>Poland</td><td>Warsaw</td><td>Zloty</td></tr><tr><td>Ireland</td><td>Dublin</td><td>Euro</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>List of African Countries, Capitals, and Currencies</h3><p>Due to the vast size and high number of countries in the African continent, several unconventional but important countries and their currencies are often asked about in exams. Below is a list of the major countries in Africa:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Country</th><th>Capital</th><th>Currency</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Egypt</td><td>Cairo</td><td>Pound</td></tr><tr><td>South Africa</td><td>Pretoria</td><td>Rand</td></tr><tr><td>Nigeria</td><td>Abuja</td><td>Naira</td></tr><tr><td>Kenya</td><td>Nairobi</td><td>Shilling</td></tr><tr><td>Ethiopia</td><td>Addis Ababa</td><td>Birr</td></tr><tr><td>Morocco</td><td>Rabat</td><td>Dirham</td></tr><tr><td>Libya</td><td>Tripoli</td><td>Dinar</td></tr><tr><td>Sudan</td><td>Khartoum</td><td>Pound</td></tr><tr><td>Uganda</td><td>Kampala</td><td>Shilling</td></tr><tr><td>Zimbabwe</td><td>Harare</td><td>US Dollar</td></tr><tr><td>Ghana</td><td>Accra</td><td>Cedi</td></tr><tr><td>Mauritius</td><td>Port Louis</td><td>Rupee</td></tr><tr><td>Algeria</td><td>Algiers</td><td>Dinar</td></tr><tr><td>Somalia</td><td>Mogadishu</td><td>Shilling</td></tr><tr><td>Tanzania</td><td>Dodoma</td><td>Shilling</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>List of North American Countries, Capitals, and Currencies</h3><p>The countries of North America are highly influential in the global economy. In particular, the currencies of countries like the USA and Canada are recognized worldwide. Below is a list of the important countries in this continent:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Country</th><th>Capital</th><th>Currency</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>United States (USA)</td><td>Washington, D.C.</td><td>US Dollar</td></tr><tr><td>Canada</td><td>Ottawa</td><td>Canadian Dollar</td></tr><tr><td>Mexico</td><td>Mexico City</td><td>Peso</td></tr><tr><td>Cuba</td><td>Havana</td><td>Peso</td></tr><tr><td>Jamaica</td><td>Kingston</td><td>Jamaican Dollar</td></tr><tr><td>Panama</td><td>Panama City</td><td>Balboa / USD</td></tr><tr><td>Costa Rica</td><td>San José</td><td>Colon</td></tr><tr><td>Bahamas</td><td>Nassau</td><td>Bahamian Dollar</td></tr><tr><td>Haiti</td><td>Port-au-Prince</td><td>Gourde</td></tr><tr><td>Guatemala</td><td>Guatemala City</td><td>Quetzal</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>List of South American Countries, Capitals, and Currencies</h3><p>South American countries are known for their natural resources and football, as well as their diverse economies. In competitive exams, questions often arise regarding the currencies of this continent (especially the Peso and Real). Below is the list of important countries:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Country</th><th>Capital</th><th>Currency</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Brazil</td><td>Brasilia</td><td>Real</td></tr><tr><td>Argentina</td><td>Buenos Aires</td><td>Peso</td></tr><tr><td>Chile</td><td>Santiago</td><td>Peso</td></tr><tr><td>Colombia</td><td>Bogota</td><td>Peso</td></tr><tr><td>Paraguay</td><td>Asuncion</td><td>Guarani</td></tr><tr><td>Peru</td><td>Lima</td><td>Sol</td></tr><tr><td>Uruguay</td><td>Montevideo</td><td>Peso</td></tr><tr><td>Venezuela</td><td>Caracas</td><td>Bolivar</td></tr><tr><td>Ecuador</td><td>Quito</td><td>US Dollar</td></tr><tr><td>Bolivia</td><td>La Paz</td><td>Boliviano</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>List of Oceania Countries, Capitals, and Currencies</h3><p>Oceania or the Australian continent is primarily composed of numerous small and large islands. The names of capitals and currencies in this region can often be confusing, so they are frequently asked about in exams. Below is a list of the major countries in Oceania:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Country</th><th>Capital</th><th>Currency</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Australia</td><td>Canberra</td><td>Australian Dollar</td></tr><tr><td>New Zealand</td><td>Wellington</td><td>NZ Dollar</td></tr><tr><td>Fiji</td><td>Suva</td><td>Fijian Dollar</td></tr><tr><td>Papua New Guinea</td><td>Port Moresby</td><td>Kina</td></tr><tr><td>Samoa</td><td>Apia</td><td>Tala</td></tr><tr><td>Tonga</td><td>Nukuʻalofa</td><td>Paʻanga</td></tr><tr><td>Vanuatu</td><td>Port Vila</td><td>Vatu</td></tr><tr><td>Kiribati</td><td>Tarawa</td><td>Australian Dollar</td></tr><tr><td>Nauru</td><td>Yaren</td><td>Australian Dollar</td></tr><tr><td>Solomon Islands</td><td>Honiara</td><td>SI Dollar</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Smart Grouping of Currencies for Quick Learning</h3><p>In exams, questions are often asked about different countries sharing the same currency name. For easier memorization, major countries using the same currency are grouped together below:</p><ul><li><strong>Rupee/Taka:</strong> India, Bangladesh, Pakistan, Sri Lanka, Nepal, Mauritius, Seychelles.</li><li><strong>Euro:</strong> France, Germany, Italy, Spain, Portugal, Austria, Belgium, Greece, Finland.</li><li><strong>Dollar:</strong> USA, Canada, Australia, New Zealand, Singapore, Jamaica, Zimbabwe.</li><li><strong>Dinar:</strong> Kuwait, Iraq, Jordan, Algeria, Libya, Bahrain, Serbia.</li><li><strong>Peso:</strong> Argentina, Mexico, Chile, Colombia, Philippines, Cuba, Uruguay.</li><li><strong>Rial/Riyal:</strong> Saudi Arabia, Iran, Oman, Qatar, Brazil (Real).</li><li><strong>Pound:</strong> United Kingdom (UK), Egypt, Sudan, Syria, Lebanon.</li></ul><div class="read-more-box">
<strong>Also Check:</strong> <a href="https://examprepzone.com/list-of-nicknames-of-indian-cities/">Nicknames of Indian Cities List: 75+ Important Nicknames</a> (Updated)</div><h3>Important Q&#038;A on World Capitals and Currencies</h3><p>Here are the questions regarding world capitals and currencies that have frequently appeared in various competitive exams. Take a quick look:</p><strong>1. What is the name of the currency of Myanmar, a neighboring country of India?</strong><br>
<strong>Answer:</strong> The name of the currency of India&#8217;s neighbor Myanmar is Kyat.<br><br><strong>2. What is the name of Japan&#8217;s capital and what currency is used there?</strong><br>
<strong>Answer:</strong> The capital of Japan is Tokyo and the currency used there is the Yen.<br><br><strong>3. In how many countries is the Euro currently used as the official currency?</strong><br>
<strong>Answer:</strong> Currently, the Euro is used as the official currency in 20 countries of the European Union.<br><br><strong>4. Which country has the highest-valued currency in the world?</strong><br>
<strong>Answer:</strong> Currently, the Kuwaiti Dinar is the world&#8217;s strongest and highest-valued currency.<br><br><strong>5. What is the name of Bhutan&#8217;s currency which is equal in value to the Indian Rupee?</strong><br>
<strong>Answer:</strong> The name of Bhutan&#8217;s currency is Ngultrum, which is circulated at par with the Indian Rupee.<br><br><strong>6. What is the name of the administrative capital of South Africa?</strong><br>
<strong>Answer:</strong> The name of the administrative capital of South Africa is Pretoria.<br><br><strong>7. What is the name of Russia&#8217;s currency?</strong><br>
<strong>Answer:</strong> The official currency of Russia is the Ruble.<br><br><strong>8. What is the name of Israel&#8217;s capital?</strong><br>
<strong>Answer:</strong> The name of Israel&#8217;s capital is Jerusalem.<br><br><strong>9. What is the name of Thailand&#8217;s currency?</strong><br>
<strong>Answer:</strong> The national currency of Thailand is the Baht.<br><br><strong>10. What is the name of Turkey&#8217;s capital?</strong><br>
<strong>Answer:</strong> The name of the capital of Turkey is Ankara.<br><br><strong>11. What is the name of the currency of the United Arab Emirates (UAE)?</strong><br>
<strong>Answer:</strong> The name of the currency of the United Arab Emirates or UAE is Dirham.<br><br><strong>12. Where is the capital of Austria located and what is its currency?</strong><br>
<strong>Answer:</strong> The capital of Austria is located in Vienna and the country&#8217;s current currency is the Euro.<br><br><strong>13. What is the name of Cuba&#8217;s currency?</strong><br>
<strong>Answer:</strong> The name of the currency used in Cuba is the Cuban Peso.<br><br><strong>14. What is the name of the Maldives&#8217; currency?</strong><br>
<strong>Answer:</strong> The name of the currency of the Maldives is Rufiyaa.<br><br><strong>15. What is the name of Indonesia&#8217;s new capital?</strong><br>
<strong>Answer:</strong> The name of the newly built capital of Indonesia is Nusantara.<br><br><strong>16. What is the name of Argentina&#8217;s currency?</strong><br>
<strong>Answer:</strong> The name of the currency of Argentina is the Argentine Peso.<br><br><strong>17. What is the official currency of China?</strong><br>
<strong>Answer:</strong> The official currency of China is the Renminbi, and its unit is called the Yuan.<br><br><strong>18. What is the name of Switzerland&#8217;s currency?</strong><br>
<strong>Answer:</strong> The name of the currency of Switzerland is the Swiss Franc.<br><br><strong>19. What is the name of Poland&#8217;s capital?</strong><br>
<strong>Answer:</strong> The name of the capital of Poland is Warsaw.<br><br><strong>20. Which country uses the Krona as its currency?</strong><br>
<strong>Answer:</strong> Krona is primarily the currency name for Nordic countries like Iceland, Sweden, or Denmark (for example, Iceland&#8217;s currency is called the Icelandic Króna).<br><br><div class="google-style-faq"><h3 class="faq-main-title">People also ask (FAQs)</h3>
<details class="faq-row"><summary class="faq-header">Which country has the strongest or most valuable currency in the world?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>Currently, the Kuwaiti Dinar (KWD) is the strongest currency in the world.</p></div></details>
<details class="faq-row"><summary class="faq-header">Which countries use the Euro as their currency?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>The Euro is the official currency of 20 European Union countries, including notable ones like France, Germany, Italy, and Spain.</p></div></details>
<details class="faq-row"><summary class="faq-header">What are the names of the currencies of India&#8217;s neighboring countries?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>Bangladesh (Taka), Pakistan (Rupee), Nepal (Rupee), Sri Lanka (Rupee), Bhutan (Ngultrum), and Myanmar (Kyat).</p></div></details>
<details class="faq-row"><summary class="faq-header">What is the official name of China&#8217;s currency?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>The official name of China&#8217;s currency is Renminbi (RMB), while its unit is called the Yuan.</p></div></details>
<details class="faq-row"><summary class="faq-header">What is the capital and currency of Brazil?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>The capital of Brazil is Brasilia and the currency is the Real.</p></div></details>
<details class="faq-row"><summary class="faq-header">What is the name of the capital of Ukraine?</summary><div class="faq-body"><p>The capital of Ukraine is Kyiv.</p></div></details></div> <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [
